(5088370, 739161, 97672, '<td valign="top">its a roof at my house i thought it was funny that no one thought it could be the roof but it was cool that people knew it was a type of plaster and it took me 2 days to find somthing if you look at it clode enough it looks like a person whearing a skarf i  was going to pull out the features but my photo editor was fritzy<br/></td>', 'its a roof at my house i thought it was funny that no one thought it could be the roof but it was cool that people knew it was a type of plaster and it took me 2 days to find somthing if you look at it clode enough it looks like a person whearing a skarf i  was going to pull out the features but my photo editor was fritzy', '2008-11-28 11:13:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5088371, 739956, 34192, '<td valign="top">I think this is pretty cool.  I guess the votes were the result of people who voted down because they knew what it was or didn''t like the applied filter.  Such is life.  You composed excellently - keep experimenting - you''ve got a good eye for shape.</td>', 'I think this is pretty cool.  I guess the votes were the result of people who voted down because they knew what it was or didn''t like the applied filter.  Such is life.  You composed excellently - keep experimenting - you''ve got a good eye for shape.', '2008-11-28 11:14:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5088502, 740346, 16154, '<td valign="top">Looks like your back! Good Job!</td>', 'Looks like your back! Good Job!', '2008-11-28 12:18:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5088578, 740346, 73564, '<td valign="top">Great job! Congrats!!!</td>', 'Great job! Congrats!!!', '2008-11-28 13:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5089297, 740315, 86447, '<td valign="top">I think it''s pretty cool... gave it a five because it''s not really greatly in focus, but is still very interesting and well composed.  I feel your pain, though, Shez... my "Benches" shot is at 4.x...  *sigh*</td>', 'I think it''s pretty cool... gave it a five because it''s not really greatly in focus, but is still very interesting and well composed.  I feel your pain, though, Shez... my "Benches" shot is at 4.x...  *sigh*', '2008-11-28 21:40:24.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5091280, 740308, 5391, '<td valign="top">Astonishingly beautiful image.  I like the contrast of the image sharpness with the murky texture that the oil has.  It looks like it goes on forever.</td>', 'Astonishingly beautiful image.  I like the contrast of the image sharpness with the murky texture that the oil has.  It looks like it goes on forever.', '2008-11-30 11:43:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5092153, 740002, 69668, '<td valign="top">Congrats Jason...another great image from you.</td>', 'Congrats Jason...another great image from you.', '2008-11-30 23:37:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5097525, 740345, 99924, '<td valign="top">I love the brightness of the green and the way it stands out against the blue background.  Congrats on the second place finish!</td>', 'I love the brightness of the green and the way it stands out against the blue background.  Congrats on the second place finish!', '2008-12-02 10:34:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5098300, 740332, 84438, '<td valign="top">This really stood out to me during the challenge; I really thought this was going to be a ribbon contender.  I gave it an 8.</td>', 'This really stood out to me during the challenge; I really thought this was going to be a ribbon contender.  I gave it an 8.', '2008-12-02 14:50:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5099067, 740237, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from critique club :)<br/> <br/>Veeeeery tight DOF, cool. Nice colors, technically good. My problems with this photo are the angle of the composition, crop could be done better and drop could be straighter... and I believe post process is a bit overdone.<br/> <br/>5.5 almost 5.6 is about right for this picture. I probably would give 5 or 4, and I would guessed overall would be around 5.2 5.3 tops.<br/> <br/>Practice practice practice.<br/> <br/>Good luck on your future challenges, never give up :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from critique club :) Veeeeery tight DOF, cool. Nice colors, technically good. My problems with this photo are the angle of the composition, crop could be done better and drop could be straighter... and I believe post process is a bit overdone. 5.5 almost 5.6 is about right for this picture. I probably would give 5 or 4, and I would guessed overall would be around 5.2 5.3 tops. Practice practice practice. Good luck on your future challenges, never give up :) Leo', '2008-12-02 19:32:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5099089, 740349, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from critique club :)<br/> <br/>Nice. I believe if you did have everything sharp instead of out of focus area on the right, it would look better.<br/> <br/>I like the colors. Very cool colors. crop is ok but I think I would either crop it more on top, or give more space to even top with bottom.<br/> <br/>I would give around 7 if I did vote, and I believe 5.7 is about right for overall score. Vignette border and a bit more image processing (not whole a lot) could get you bit more score... then again, it''s my personal opinion :P<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work, you do have the talent, need some more practice :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from critique club :) Nice. I believe if you did have everything sharp instead of out of focus area on the right, it would look better. I like the colors. Very cool colors. crop is ok but I think I would either crop it more on top, or give more space to even top with bottom. I would give around 7 if I did vote, and I believe 5.7 is about right for overall score. Vignette border and a bit more image processing (not whole a lot) could get you bit more score... then again, it''s my personal opinion :P Keep up the good work, you do have the talent, need some more practice :) Leo', '2008-12-02 19:43:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5099132, 739822, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from critique club :)<br/> <br/>5.0 little low for this. I thought it was some prints on sand or something. Nice lights there, very interesting. B&amp;W I think one of the things killed it. Burn area on the leaf also point taker.<br/> <br/>Technically nice, compositing is nice. You know this is not a top of the line photo, but you did good job. You came up with something interesting. My first entry was 4 something, so, you already did good start.<br/> <br/>Keep on practicing and entering challenges, I have a feeling you might get a ribbon soon :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from critique club :) 5.0 little low for this. I thought it was some prints on sand or something. Nice lights there, very interesting. B&W I think one of the things killed it. Burn area on the leaf also point taker. Technically nice, compositing is nice. You know this is not a top of the line photo, but you did good job. You came up with something interesting. My first entry was 4 something, so, you already did good start. Keep on practicing and entering challenges, I have a feeling you might get a ribbon soon :) Leo', '2008-12-02 19:54:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5099909, 739748, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from critique club :)<br/> <br/>Last minute idea?! that''s a very good idea. I thought it was a ring. For sure, this is not a 6.0 shot... easily 6.4 or 6.6 range. Some people I tell ya :P<br/> <br/>I have not much to say about this, but still, since I am in critique club and your photo came to me as next one... let me do my job.<br/> <br/>Technically: Perfect<br/>Composition: perfect<br/>Idea: perfect<br/>Challenge worthy: 100%<br/> <br/>ok, I am done.<br/> <br/>Sorry pal, but if you need negative critique, you should ask again, I can''t find anything wrong with this photo :P<br/> <br/>You do have the equipment and you know places, so it seems from your page, and I don''t understand, with all that good stuff, you only have one ribbon. As your superior (I think critique club members like generals or something you know) I order you to get more ribbons... NOW.<br/> <br/>Ok, keep up the good work. Watch for hot spots on your photos. It very well might be your camera, but you do have little problems with 1-shutter speed 2-iso 3-aparture. Keep them in balanced ;)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from critique club :) Last minute idea?! that''s a very good idea. I thought it was a ring. For sure, this is not a 6.0 shot... easily 6.4 or 6.6 range. Some people I tell ya :P I have not much to say about this, but still, since I am in critique club and your photo came to me as next one... let me do my job. Technically: PerfectComposition: perfectIdea: perfectChallenge worthy: 100% ok, I am done. Sorry pal, but if you need negative critique, you should ask again, I can''t find anything wrong with this photo :P You do have the equipment and you know places, so it seems from your page, and I don''t understand, with all that good stuff, you only have one ribbon. As your superior (I think critique club members like generals or something you know) I order you to get more ribbons... NOW. Ok, keep up the good work. Watch for hot spots on your photos. It very well might be your camera, but you do have little problems with 1-shutter speed 2-iso 3-aparture. Keep them in balanced ;) Leo', '2008-12-02 22:55:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5099949, 740211, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from critique club :)<br/> <br/>Jon, I will be honest as I can be with you. I recognize talent when I see one and you are definitely one of them. Here are the things I like about your work,<br/> <br/>1-Ideas<br/>2-Imagination<br/>3-Execution of your imaginations<br/>4-Composition<br/> <br/>What else left for you to get ribbons?<br/> <br/>1-A better camera (this is a joke, haha), I love 30Ds<br/> <br/>I think you need to find better subjects? I don''t know. It probably and most likely practice practice practice situation. More photos you take and enter, better you will get, and I tell you one thing, you will get better quicker than others.<br/> <br/>For this photo, I think you got 5.0 ( I mean good score) for the fame :\ Don''t get me wrong, as I said, close to a perfect image but not too interesting. You also missed a white spot on the middle, should give a bit more angle... DOF is ok, I think I would probably keep the same amount. But frame goes pretty well with the overall photo. I think you got your 0.3 or 0.5 range from the frame. I definitely voted 5 or 6 though.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work; try as much as you can and you will start 6+ s very soon :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from critique club :) Jon, I will be honest as I can be with you. I recognize talent when I see one and you are definitely one of them. Here are the things I like about your work, 1-Ideas2-Imagination3-Execution of your imaginations4-Composition What else left for you to get ribbons? 1-A better camera (this is a joke, haha), I love 30Ds I think you need to find better subjects? I don''t know. It probably and most likely practice practice practice situation. More photos you take and enter, better you will get, and I tell you one thing, you will get better quicker than others. For this photo, I think you got 5.0 ( I mean good score) for the fame :\ Don''t get me wrong, as I said, close to a perfect image but not too interesting. You also missed a white spot on the middle, should give a bit more angle... DOF is ok, I think I would probably keep the same amount. But frame goes pretty well with the overall photo. I think you got your 0.3 or 0.5 range from the frame. I definitely voted 5 or 6 though. Keep up the good work; try as much as you can and you will start 6+ s very soon :) Leo', '2008-12-02 23:16:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5099983, 740114, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from critique club :)<br/> <br/>Nice photo. Meets the challenge, but I am not here for that...<br/> <br/>Technically, good photo. Good lights and exposure. Not too sharp, little rainbow affects which gives a blurry feeling to my eyes (strange). Nice compositing, tight and clean image.<br/> <br/>If I voted, I would give 5 or 6 to this photo, and 5.1 overall score is about right.<br/> <br/>i checked your page, you do have this "photographer''s eyes" thing, you see things the way normal people wouldn''t see most likely. So, keep on clicking, you will be one of the big shots, oh maybe a year or two (if not sooner) here in DPC.<br/> <br/>Never give-up, and develop a thick skin... I don''t know why I said that but it is my suggestion to you :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from critique club :) Nice photo. Meets the challenge, but I am not here for that... Technically, good photo. Good lights and exposure. Not too sharp, little rainbow affects which gives a blurry feeling to my eyes (strange). Nice compositing, tight and clean image. If I voted, I would give 5 or 6 to this photo, and 5.1 overall score is about right. i checked your page, you do have this "photographer''s eyes" thing, you see things the way normal people wouldn''t see most likely. So, keep on clicking, you will be one of the big shots, oh maybe a year or two (if not sooner) here in DPC. Never give-up, and develop a thick skin... I don''t know why I said that but it is my suggestion to you :) Leo', '2008-12-02 23:27:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5101339, 740211, 98948, '<td valign="top">Leo,<br/> <br/>Thank you for taking the time to critique this photo, I really appreciate it. My two greatest challenges right now are coming up with ideas and having the time to pursue photography. I ceartainly appreciate the opportunity that DPC offers in inspiring creativity. The feedback, particularly detailed feedback such as yours, is invaluable. Thank you very much for that.<br/> <br/>Take care... J</td>', 'Leo, Thank you for taking the time to critique this photo, I really appreciate it. My two greatest challenges right now are coming up with ideas and having the time to pursue photography. I ceartainly appreciate the opportunity that DPC offers in inspiring creativity. The feedback, particularly detailed feedback such as yours, is invaluable. Thank you very much for that. Take care... J', '2008-12-03 10:34:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5105175, 740178, 90658, '<td valign="top">Hey, I know that shoehorn :)<br/> <br/>See you can "shoehorn" something and get a reasonable score :)<br/> <br/>No, really, I thought it was a cup on a miniture golf course, so well-done.</td>', 'Hey, I know that shoehorn :) See you can "shoehorn" something and get a reasonable score :) No, really, I thought it was a cup on a miniture golf course, so well-done.', '2008-12-04 10:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
